    "event_story": {
      "type": "rizo-text",
      "settings": {
        "style": "body",
        "label": "From the table",
        "heading": "The community showed up for us.",
        "body": "<p>The most recent WPSD day had plenty go wrong before we got there. Last-minute supplies, a fundraiser, a new ride, figuring out who was in charge of what.</p><p>Then people started helping. One kid went home and brought us Ziploc bags because we needed them. A woman running her own table kept checking on us, giving pointers and taking our pictures. Aiden had the table set up before I arrived and spent the day helping kids make shirts.</p><p>I was scared out of my mind. It was also the first time I really felt like a boss. The kids had fun. The community made us feel like we belonged there.</p>",
        "align": "offset",
        "surface": "solid",
        "space": "m",
        "fog": 0
      }
    },
    "seen": {
      "type": "rizo-text",
      "settings": {
        "style": "quote",
        "label": "",
        "body": "<p>Whenever somebody tells me they saw someone in Rizo, I always ask: Who? What did they look like? Where?</p>",
        "cite": "Taymar Spencer",
        "align": "offset",
        "surface": "open",
        "space": "l",
        "fog": 25
      }
    },
